  "summary_text": "Kyle,\n\nPort Washington is performing to plan\u2014call it structurally sound. Yesterday's 19% revenue dip was purely a capacity play: you ran 5 groomers against a trailing baseline of 5, but that's still down from the prior Thursday's implicit 6\u20137 groomer equivalent (back-calculating from $3,700 core groom revenue). The real signal is positive: your $/groomer-day held flat at $500, add-on attach improved to 56%, and month-to-date you're tracking 0.5% above DOW-adjusted expectation. Retail sagged 28%\u2014worth a front-of-house check, but grooming productivity is driving the engine. Year-to-date you're up 36% appointments and 36% revenue, a clean signal that the market is there. One concern: X-Small Treat Tables and Jack&Pup Braided Bully 12\" are out of stock\u2014reorder immediately before Saturday volume hits.\n\nHicksville is a mixed picture. Yesterday grooming revenue jumped 10% week-over-week and you're up 16% month-to-date against DOW-adjusted expectation, which is genuinely strong. But retail collapsed 59%, a structural miss that suggests front-of-house discipline has slipped. More pressing: your $/groomer-day is $369 against a trailing baseline of $403\u2014you're running cooler despite yesterday's 4-groomer slate. Week-to-date you're down 11% appointments, and MTD groomer-days haven't budged (2.8/day vs 2.6 prior)\u2014this location is under-capacity relative to demand. That $369 productivity suggests either a mix shift or booking softness. No bather hours scheduled or available is also a constraint; you're leaving margin on the table.\n\nGlen Cove is a bright spot\u2014up 154% yesterday and 34% above expectation month-to-date\u2014but it's also a fragile asset. You have zero groomer-days scheduled for the next 7 days. That's not sustainable. Julianne and Melanie are performing at baseline, but without scheduled coverage, you'll hemorrhage the momentum you've just built. Treat this as a scheduling emergency.\n\n**Capacity & coverage:** Port Washington has 6 groomer-days today (6 floor, 15h bathers) and 4 tomorrow; Hicksville has 5 today and 4 tomorrow; Glen Cove has 0 today and tomorrow\u2014fix this now; next 7 days total 58 groomer-days across all locations."
